1. Align repo-content resolver with 3 new file lists
    [x] 'content/backend/core/core/entities.py': Add user_selected_files, assistant_selected_files, meta_files (default empty) to RepoContentResolver; keep expanded_paths intact
        - fields are list[str] with default_factory=list
        - assistant_selected_files stays empty (populated later)
    [x] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/validators/fileset_validator.py': Populate user_selected_files and meta_files for each RepoContentResolver using pud_content_assets.paths (no new DiskPort)
        - resolve content_fileset includes/excludes → user_selected_files
        - resolve meta_fileset includes/excludes → meta_files
        - leave assistant_selected_files empty
    [x] 'content/backend/render_pipeline/render_service.py': Process repo content in order — user_selected_files (full), assistant_selected_files (full), meta_files (metadata); keep expanded_paths
        - in _res_repo_content, for each path in prompt.expanded_paths: if present in meta_files, remove it and append to assistant_selected_files; otherwise ignore
        - drop the per-fileset disk globbing in _res_repo_content
    [x] 'content/backend/asset_ingestion/ingestion_service.py': _build_resolver reads user_selected_files, assistant_selected_files, meta_files from the input dict
        - parse only when present; keep expanded_paths as-is
    [x] 'content/backend/adapters/disk_adapter.py': get_dir_manifest should return only actual file paths, not empty directory entries
        - in the `rel_roots is None` branch: drop the `or (sub_path.is_dir() and not any(sub_path.iterdir()))` clause, keep only `sub_path.is_file()`
        - in the `rel_roots` (else) branch: same — the `sub_path.is_dir()` check for empty dirs should be dropped from the rglob sub-iteration; a fileset include pointing at a directory that exists with content is already covered by its descendant files
        - rationale: `get_dir_manifest` is the sole source for `pud_content_assets.paths`, which the validator uses for prefix-matching to populate `user_selected_files`/`meta_files`; empty dirs in the manifest cause `IsADirectoryError` at render time when the service calls `get_file_contents` on a directory path

